S,G|INT. BUS - (DAY) - MED. CLOSE SHOT
O|
N|Tired of watching the sameness of the desert, Hank
N|grows, restless. He looks about for something to do.
N|Ben leans back against the seat and closes his eyes.
N|Jo takes a paper-bound novel out of her bag, finds her
N|place. Hank decides to wander down the aisle of the
N|bus and test its possibilities for adventure.
O|
N,G|The CAMERA DOLLIES BACK with him as he rather aimlessly
N|makes for the front of the bus,. Having left the Arab
N|village, the bus picks up speed, and is beginning to
N|bump and sway somewhat. When Hank is a little better
N|than half way down the aisle, the bus sways in a
N|particularly startling manner, causing Hank to stagger.
N|In order to steady himself, he thrusts out his hand to
N|grab the side of a seat. He misses the seat, and only
N|succeeds in clutching at the veil of an Arab woman.
N|Unfortunately, he pulls the veil from her face.
O|
O|
S,G|INT. BUS - (DAY) - CLOSE SHOT
O|
N|The startled woman, instantly horrified, covers her
N|face with her hands and gives a sharp cry,
O|
O|
S,G|INT. BUS - (DAY) - CLOSE SHOT
O|
N|With the bus still bumping and swaying, Hank staggers
N|a bit without realizing that he still has, hold of the
N|woman's veil.
O|
